## Rationale
social_routes.py and social_workflow_routes.py were writing to artifacts/Sweet-Pea-Rudi19/social/social_media.db which doesn't exist — every social API call returns 503. This routes through get_connection() → Postgres and creates the social tables on first use. Tables are prefixed with social_ to avoid collision with future tables in the shared schema.

## Risk Assessment
  Risk Level: LOW
  Reversible: YES — social_media.db doesn't exist, no data at risk
  Dependencies: core.db.get_connection() must be importable from api/ context. _ensure_social_tables runs once on first request.
  Note: Social tables will start empty. Seed data from governance/scripts/create_social_media_db.py should be ported separately (follow-up task).
  Note: Table name prefix changed: posts → social_posts, etc. to avoid collision with general knowledge concepts.
